    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d370">

                <pb facs="0531" n="435" xml:id="pg435"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/25054: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Poland</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-06-27T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 27, 1921—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>150. Legation’s telegram No. 146, dated June 23, 5 p.m. Advise the Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs confidentially that Department highly appreciates the attitude
                    which his Government has taken, and add that this Government has not yet
                    extended recognition. The outlook now is that there will be a delay in
                    recognition. You should receive very shortly a full statement outlining the
                    position of the Department which was given to the public on the 7th of
                        June,<anchor n="52" xml:id="d370-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d370-f1" n="52" xml:id="d370-f1-content">
                <p>Quoted in telegram no. 85, June 8, 1921, to the Chargé in Mexico, <ref
                        target="#pg406">p. 406</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
